nts covered:\n\n- \\(L_{s}\\): \\((1,1),\\;(2,2)\\);\n- \\(L_{v}\\): \\((1,2),\\;(1,3)\\);\n- \\(L_{h}\\): \\((2,1),\\;(3,1)\\).\n\nThese are exactly the six points required for \\(n=3\\). Hence every point \\((a,b)\\) with \\(a,b\\ge 1\\) and \\(a+b\\le 4\\) lies on at least one of the three lines.\n\n**Count of sunny lines.**  \nAmong the three lines only \\(L_{s}\\) is sunny; \\(L_{v}\\) and \\(L_{h}\\) are not. Thus the configuration contains exactly  \n\n\\[\nk = 1\n\\]\n\nsunny line.\n\nTherefore, for \\(n=3\\) the integer \\(k=1\\) is realizable. \\(\\boxed{k=1}\\)"
